**Thought summary of the work completed**

I inspected `ProcessorTemplateHandler.handleOpenElement(...)` and its collaborators (`TemplateModelController`, `OpenElementTag`, `ElementDefinitions`, `TemplateFlowController`, `GatheringModelProcessable`, `IteratedGatheringModelProcessable`, `OpenElementTagModelProcessable`, `EngineContext`, `TemplateData`) and then built a direct-call test harness in package `org.thymeleaf.engine` (giving access to package-private types like `OpenElementTag`, `Attributes`, `ElementDefinitions`, `TemplateFlowController`).

Harness design:
- `ElementDefinitions(new EnumMap<TemplateMode, Set<IElementProcessor>>...)` + `forName(HTML, "div")` produces an element definition carrying exactly the processors under test (including deliberately invalid ones).
- `new OpenElementTag(HTML, def, "div", attributes, false)` builds engine tags with/without attributes.
- `EngineContext` + `TemplateData` + real `TemplateEngine` configuration (`setContext`) drive the handler; a `RecordingTemplateHandler` (`ITemplateHandler`) records every delegated event; a second engine configuration with a custom dialect (uppercasing `AbstractTextProcessor`) distinguishes "processable" queues (routed through the handler) from plain delegation.
- I added a **test-scoped** `org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter` dependency to `lib/thymeleaf/pom.xml` (version managed by the existing `junit-bom` import) — the only non-test-file change.

The generated suite (25 tests, all green: `Tests run: 25, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`) covers:
- fast-fail delegation for elements without processors (same event instance delegated);
- processor precedence ordering and `setAttribute`/`removeAttribute` effects on the delegated tag;
- local variables applied to the engine context;
- `setBody` text/model replacement + body skipping + close-tag still processed;
- non-processable vs processable queues (raw text vs text processed by text processors);
- `replaceWith` text/model (element, body and close tag discarded);
- `removeElement`, `removeTags`, `removeBody`, `removeAllButFirstChild` (first child only);
- `insertBefore` / `insertImmediatelyAfter` delegation ordering;
- element model processors: suspension while gathering, unchanged-model normal delegation, modified-model replacement of the whole element, and `TemplateProcessingException` when a prior processor already modified the body;
- iteration (`iterateElement`) delegating the element once per item and exposing iteration variables;
- throttling: `queueEvent` path (nothing delegated, no processor executed, then `handlePending()`), `queueProcessable` path (model queued mid-processing, then resumed), and immediate processing when throttling is enabled but not stopped;
- `IllegalStateException` for an `IElementProcessor` that is neither a tag nor a model processor.

**Important note:** after the final successful test run, the execution container died (`Error response from daemon: No such container: 055d557bb...`) and every subsequent command — including the required submission command `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` — fails with that daemon error, so I cannot re-verify or submit from the shell. The last executed, verified state of the repository is: `lib/thymeleaf/src/test/java/org/thymeleaf/engine/ProcessorTemplateHandlerHandleOpenElementTests.java` (complete suite, 25/25 passing) plus the test-scoped JUnit dependency in `lib/thymeleaf/pom.xml`; no production sources were modified.

